ables","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"Inferno, I, 32","pagenum":"273","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"Paradiso, XXXI, 108","pagenum":"274","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"Ragnarök","pagenum":"276","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"Parable of Cervantes and the Quixote","pagenum":"278","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"The Witness","pagenum":"279","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"A Problem","pagenum":"280","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"Borges and I","pagenum":"282","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":1,"title":"Everything and Nothing","pagenum":"284","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"Elegy","pagenum":"287","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-02-27T19:57:47.313417"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-04-27T00:00:52.079054"}}},"ISBN:9780811200127":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780811200127","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL35262933M/Labyrinths","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL35262933M/Labyrinths","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12077329-S.jpg","details":{"identifiers":{"wikidata":["Q118967977"]},"title":"Labyrinths","subtitle":"Selected Stories & Other Writings","publish_date":"1970?","publishers":["New Directions Publishing Corporation"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publish_places":["New York"],"copyright_date":"1964","edition_name":"Augmented edition, tenth printing","pagination":"241p.","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"covers":[12077329],"local_id":["urn:scms:0188500514644","urn:nuls:31786000092459"],"source_records":["marc:marc_scms/20220805_ADAM_MARC_records.mrc:121391337:1573","marc:marc_nuls/NULS_PHC_180925.mrc:205214562:1027","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:397075976:1449","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-005.mrc:554117907:1192"],"key":"/books/OL35262933M","number_of_pages":241,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL110959W"}],"classifications":{},"isbn_10":["0811200124"],"isbn_13":["9780811200127"],"lccn":["64025440","68028626"],"oclc_numbers":["87844074","1861","40233705"],"lc_classifications":["PQ7797.B635 L3 1964","HJ1011 .D6 1968"],"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-10-12T18:36:16.332270"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-07-19T17:47:38.327923"}}},"ISBN:9780811229951":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780811229951","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL47068047M/Labyrinths","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL47068047M/Labyrinths","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13379270-S.jpg","details":{"works":[{"key":"/works/OL110959W"}],"title":"Labyrinths","publishers":["New Directions"],"publish_date":"2019","key":"/books/OL47068047M","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["90589329"]},"covers":[13379270],"isbn_13":["9780811229951"],"isbn_10":["0811229955"],"classifications":{},"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The groundbreaking trans-genre work of Argentinian writer Jorge Luis Borges (1899-1986) has been insinuating itself into the structure, stance, and very breath of world literature for well over half a century. Multi-layered, self-referential, elusive, and allusive writing is now frequently labeled Borgesian. Umberto Eco’s international bestseller, The Name of the Rose, is, on one level, an elaborate improvisation on Borges’ fiction “The Library,” which American readers first encountered in the original 1962 New Directions publication of Labyrinths. This new edition of Labyrinths, the classic representative selection of Borges’ writing edited by Donald A. Yates and James E. Irby (in translations by themselves and others), includes the text of the original edition (as augmented in 1964) as well as Irby’s biographical and critical essay, a poignant tribute by Andre Maurois, and a chronology of the author’s life. Borges enthusiast William Gibson has contributed a new introduction bringing Borges’ influence and importance into the twenty-first century."},"physical_format":"Digital Audio","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"latest_revision":3,"revision":3,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-03-05T08:16:10.432720"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-03-05T08:17:10.538459"}}},"ISBN:9780670823932":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780670823932","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18369318M/The_book_of_fantasy","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18369318M/The_book_of_fantasy","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5416510-S.jpg","details":{"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Translation of: Antologia de la literatura fantastica.\n\nIncludes bio-bibliographies."},"identifiers":{"librarything":["52706"],"goodreads":["80477"]},"title":"The book of fantasy","publishers":["Viking"],"covers":[5416510,4067755],"lc_classifications":["PN6071.F25  A5513 1988","PN6071.F25 A5513 1988","PN6071.F25A5513 1988"],"publish_places":["New York, NY"],"contributions":["Borges, Jorge Luis,  1899-","Ocampo, Silvina.","Bioy Casares, Adolfo."],"subjects":["Fantastic literature."],"pagination":"384 p. ; ","source_records":["amazon:0670823937","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part18.utf8:180122696:887","bwb:9780670823932","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-003.mrc:29790962:1403"],"work_titles":["Antologia de la literatura fantastica.  English."],"lccn":["88040100"],"isbn_10":["0670823937"],"dewey_decimal_class":["808.83/876 "],"by_statement":"edited by Jorge Luis Borges, Silvina Ocampo, A. Bioy Casares ; introduced by Ursula K. Le Guin.","oclc_numbers":["17803482"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"key":"/books/OL18369318M","number_of_pages":384,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL16538128W"}],"publish_date":"1988","latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-10-16T10:07:23.211653"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-07-17T22:53:30.670807"}}},"ISBN:9780881846560":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780881846560","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL1880269M/The_Book_of_Fantasy","preview":"borrow","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/bookoffantasy00borg","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10832276-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Carroll & Graf"],"ia_box_id":["IA171801"],"covers":[10832276],"key":"/books/OL1880269M","publish_places":["New York"],"contributions":["Borges, Jorge Luis, 1899-","Ocampo, Silvina.","Bioy Casares, Adolfo."],"work_title":["Antología de la literatura fantástica. English."],"pagination":"384p.","classifications":{},"source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part21.dat:84782455:885","marc:marc_loc_updates/v37.i38.records.utf8:4409795:894","ia:bookoffantasy00borg","amazon:0881846562","bwb:9780881846560"],"title":"The Book of Fantasy","notes":"Translation of: Antología de la literatura fantástica.","identifiers":{"librarything":["52706"],"goodreads":["44051"],"amazon":["0881846562"],"google":["5XgtGwAACAAJ"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["Fantasy literature"],"publish_date":"1990","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"edited by Jorge Luis Borges, Silvina Ocampo, A. Bioy Casares ; introduced by Ursula K. Le Guin.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL16538128W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"edition_name":"1st English-language edition, revised and expanded","description":"The Book of Fantasy began one night when three friends fell to talking about fantasies and ghost stories. The place was Buenos Aires, 1937, and the people were Jorge Luis Borges, Adolfo Bioy Casares and his wife Silvina debated which stories were best, wrote Bioy Casares later, 'and someone suggested that if we brought together the tales and the fragments that we had listed in our notebooks we would have a good book. '\r\n\r\nThe result is an astonishing collection of stories drawn from all the literatures of the world from Ancient China to Modern America mingling the obscure and the neglected with the already famous and showing a splendid disdain for conventional literary opinion. Among the authors included are Leonid Andreyev, Léon Bloy, Lewis Carroll, Jean Cocteau, O.K. Chesterton, James Joyce, Giovanni Papini, Carlos Peralta and Villiers de L'lsle Adam, some of whom have never been translated before. 'It is some- times said, wrote Bruce Chatwin. 'that all the elements of civilization end up eventually in Argentina, and most of it ends up in Borges' head. His values are those of high Western civilization They say lives in a world of imagination and dreams, but he's central to life. '\r\n\r\nNow considerably expanded and published for the first time in English, The Book of Fantasy has a specially-written introduction by Ursula K. Le Guin. twice winner of both the Hugo and Nebula awards. She writes: 'It is an idiosyncratic selection. and completely eclectic. of the stories will be familiar to anyone who reads, others are exotic discoveries. A very well-known piece ... seems less predictable set among works and fragments from the Orient and South America and distant centuries, by Kafka Swedeolorg Cortäzar, Akutagawa. Niu Chiao; its own essential strangeness is restored to This is, quite simply, the finest anthology of its kind.\r\n--back cover","translated_from":[{"key":"/languages/spa"}],"number_of_pages":384,"translation_of":"Antología de la literatura fantástica","copyright_date":"1988","physical_format":"Paperback","ocaid":"bookoffantasy00borg","isbn_10":["0881846562"],"isbn_13":["9780881846560"],"lccn":["90040770"],"oclc_numbers":["21971251"],"dewey_decimal_class":["808.83/8766"],"lc_classifications":["PN6071.F25 A5713 1990","PN6071.F25A5713 1990"],"latest_revision":14,"revision":14,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime"